`moreButtonAction` is now `@Sendable @MainActor`, and then gets wrapped in a non-Sendable `@MainActor` closure just to pass it to `ActionButtonViewModel.touchUpAction`, which is typed `(@MainActor (UIButton) -> Void)?`.

::code{file="firefox-ios/Client/Frontend/Home/Homepage/SectionHeader/LabelButtonHeaderView.swift" lines="95-113"}

A `@Sendable` closure already converts implicitly to the non-Sendable function type, so the wrapper isn't needed. It also has a small side effect: when `moreButtonAction` is `nil`, `touchUpAction` becomes a non-nil no-op closure, so any `touchUpAction == nil` check would behave differently. The client app target isn't being migrated in this PR, and the only callers (`HomepageViewController`) pass `[weak self]` closures that work either way. The simplest fix is to revert this file or pass `moreButtonAction` straight through.

::suggestion{file="firefox-ios/Client/Frontend/Home/Homepage/SectionHeader/LabelButtonHeaderView.swift" lines="106-113"}
